# Claude CLI Rules - Multi-Branch SaaS Platform

## Project Context
Multi-branch SaaS platform dengan Next.js 16+, Supabase, Prisma untuk branch management dan RBAC.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 16+ (App Router)
- TypeScript (strict mode)
- Supabase (Auth + Database)
- Prisma ORM
- shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS
- React Hook Form + Zod
- TanStack Query

## Code Style & Conventions

### File Naming
- Components: PascalCase (e.g., `UserForm.tsx`)
- Utilities/Actions: kebab-case (e.g., `create-user.ts`)
- Types: kebab-case (e.g., `user.types.ts`)

### Folder Structure
```
features/
  [domain]/
    actions/     # Server Actions
    components/  # React Components
    hooks/       # Custom Hooks
    services/    # Business Logic
    types/       # Type Definitions
```

### TypeScript Rules
- Always use strict mode
- Prefer type over interface for simple types
- Use Zod for runtime validation
- Export types from domain types/index.ts

### React/Next.js Rules
- Use Server Components by default
- Add "use client" only when needed (forms, hooks, interactivity)
- Prefer Server Actions over API routes
- Use Suspense boundaries for loading states

### Database Rules
- Use Prisma for all database operations
- Always use transactions for multi-table operations
- Implement RLS policies in Supabase
- Use connection pooling for production

### Security Rules
- Never expose sensitive data in client components
- Always validate input with Zod schemas
- Use RBAC for all protected routes
- Implement rate limiting on Server Actions

## Response Format
- Jawab singkat dan langsung ke inti
- Fokus pada code generation
- Minta klarifikasi untuk detail panjang
- Pandu step-by-step, tidak semua sekaligus
- Sertakan status token di setiap response

## Current Phase
Setup foundation: Prisma Schema → Supabase Config → Auth → RBAC → User Management → Branch Management

## Project Goals
1. User management dengan role assignment
2. Branch management dengan hierarchy (HQ → Branch → Sub-branch)
3. RBAC system dengan permission checking
4. Extensible untuk features tambahan



## Workflow Commands

When I say "status", show:
1. Current task from @docs/workflow.md
2. Files being worked on
3. Next 3 tasks in queue
4. Any blockers

When I say "done [task]":
1. Mark task as completed in workflow.md
2. Add completion timestamp
3. Show next task
4. Summarize what was accomplished

When I say "next":
1. Show next task details
2. List relevant files
3. Show any dependencies
4. Suggest starting approach

When I say "checkpoint":
1. Update workflow.md with current progress
2. Add session notes with timestamp
3. List files modified in this session
4. Suggest next session focus

When I say "token", show this session token and weekly token